{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/textX","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"textX"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"text-x"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The horizontal offset specifying where the baseline of the start of the ending text appears, relative to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"start of the ending line."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding"]]},"metadata":{"title":"textX","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"textX"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLEndingV5textXSdSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","role":"symbol"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/textx"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTenths":{"title":"MXLTenths","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTenths"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tenths type is a number representing tenths of interline staff space (positive or negative). Both integer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and decimal values are allowed, such as 5 for a half space and 2.5 for a quarter space. Interline space is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured from the middle of a staff line."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTenths"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltenths"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding/textX":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/textx","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/textX","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The horizontal offset specifying where the baseline of the start of the ending text appears, relative to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"start of the ending line."}],"title":"textX","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"textX"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending","abstract":[{"text":"The ending type represents multiple (e.g. first and second) endings. Typically, the start type is associated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"downward jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"typical for second endings that do not conclude a piece. The length of the jog can be specified using the end-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length attribute. The text-x and text-y attributes are offsets that specify where the baseline of the start of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ending text appears, relative to the start of the ending line.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLEnding","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding","kind":"symbol"}}}